# Alpha Deck -- FORK environment template. `scripts/fork.sh init` copies this to `.env.fork` at the fork
# WORKTREE root (gitignored) and fills in the identity block; edit by hand only if you know why.
# Read by docker-compose.fork.yml via `--env-file .env.fork` (${VAR} interpolation) AND injected into the
# containers for the keys the base compose file forwards. Full model: docs/FORKS.md.

# --- Fork identity (filled by `fork.sh init`; the wrapper + refresh-fork.sh validate these) ----------
# FORK_NAME drives EVERYTHING: project alphadeck_<name>, DB alphadeck_<name>, volumes alphadeck_<name>_*.
# Lowercase [a-z0-9_]+ only; the tooling REFUSES empty/prod/dev/sig/test (fail-closed -- a misconfigured
# fork must die loudly, never resolve to prod).
FORK_NAME=
# The port slot: slot N -> app 808N / api 800N / pg 554(4+N). Taken: prod=0, dev=1, sig=2. Forks start
# at 3. The three ports are stored EXPLICITLY (not derived) so a raw `docker compose --env-file .env.fork`
# works without the wrapper; keep them consistent with the slot.
FORK_SLOT=
FORK_APP_PORT=
FORK_API_PORT=
FORK_PG_PORT=
# Backend image extras: `replay` bakes duckdb+pyarrow for the in-container backtest harness (the
# Signals-Lab precedent -- forks are experiment stands; backend/Dockerfile's PIP_EXTRAS ARG). Set EMPTY
# (FORK_PIP_EXTRAS=) for a lean prod-shaped image.
FORK_PIP_EXTRAS=replay

# --- The SEC EDGAR User-Agent: EMPTY ON PURPOSE ------------------------------------------------------
# A fork is structurally unable to live-fetch SEC: config is fail-open, so a BLANK UA makes the backend
# skip every live EDGAR pull (the boot log + /health say "degraded: user_agent missing" -- expected in a
# fork). New data reaches a fork by ADD-TO-PROD -> refresh: put the name in a prod thesis, let prod's cron
# fetch it, then `fork.sh refresh --reset` (docs/FORKS.md). Exactly ONE live scheduled fetcher exists:
# prod. Setting a UA here is a deliberate opt-in to ad-hoc live pulls from this fork -- know why.
ALPHADECK_USER_AGENT=

# --- LLM + data keys (all FAIL-OPEN; empty = the seam returns nothing, the app works) ----------------
# The Workbench drafters (FLAG explanations, narrative->chain) cost real API credits per draft -- in a
# fork that spend is yours to opt into, same as prod. Reusing prod's values is fine.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
POLYGON_API_KEY=

# --- OPTIONAL: everything else -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any key from .env.example works here too (the base compose file forwards them identically). The cron
# keys (ALPHADECK_CRON_*) are moot in a fork: the cron service is OFF (donotstart profile) -- a fork never
# live-fetches on a schedule and records no call-of-record (the R2a gate withholds no-live runs).
